    "body": "## Problem\n\n`watchdirs()` scans and watches every directory that is not excluded, even when a glob\nonly matches files in one subtree. Some language servers register absolute dependency\nfilenames separately. Neovim uses the workspace root for these string globs, so each\nextra registration can scan and allocate libuv handles across the whole tree.\n\n## Solution\n\nKeep each glob's literal directory prefix with its compiled matcher. A directory must be\nallowed by both the include filter and at least one watch rule. Skip unrelated subtrees,\nincluding new directories created later. Keep parent directories watched so matching\ndirectories can be found if created later. Report events only when they match the full\npatterns.\n\nFor example, watching `/project` for `/project/src/**/*.lua` watches the `src` tree and\n`/project` itself:\n\n```text\n/project/            watched\n|-- src/             watched\n|   `-- lib/         watched\n|-- tests/           skipped\n|   `-- fixtures/    skipped\n`-- vendor/          skipped\n    `-- pkg/         skipped\n```\n\nWith no exclusions, this uses three watches instead of seven.\n\nAlso fix globs beginning with `#`, so the extracted directory prefix agrees with the\npaths the glob matches.\n\n## Language server impact\n\nThe gain can be large, but depends on the server's patterns and the workspace layout.\nSeparate watches for absolute dependency filenames can skip most directories.\n\nFor example, a test workspace has 213 directories, including 201 under `build/`. The two\ndependency files in this example are under `packages/` and `styles/`, so their watches\ncan skip `build/`. Before this change, each watch starts at the workspace root, scans\nall 213 directories and creates 213 libuv handles.\n\nWith this change:\n\n- Haskell Language Server: a separate watch for `/project/packages/demo/demo.cabal`\n  watches four directories: the project root, `packages/`, `demo/` and its `src/` child.\n  This cuts that watch's scans and handles by 98%. With one broad source watch and this\n  dependency watch, the total falls by 49%.\n- Tailwind CSS v4: a separate watch for the imported `/project/styles/themes/colors.css`\n  watches three directories: the project root, `styles/` and `themes/`. This cuts that\n  watch's scans and handles by 99%. With two broad watches and this dependency watch,\n  the total falls by 33%.\n\nThe broad watches still cover all 213 directories. The saving comes from avoiding\nrepeated scans and extra handles for each dependency watch.\n\nMost servers with watch registrations in the survey do not benefit. Their patterns match\nthroughout the watch root, or their watches already start at the relevant directory. In\nboth cases, the glob prefix cannot exclude more directories.\n",
